From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilwojcik93 <adminit@adar.pl>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:52:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] posture: add client posture classifier and OS signal
 detectors

posture: add client posture classifier and OS signal detectors

Add the pure-logic half of the client posture feature: decide whether this
client is a desktop, laptop, tablet or handheld, and gather the signals that
decision needs.

postureclassifier.{h,cpp} is deliberately free of OS and Qt GUI calls so it can
be unit tested everywhere. It classifies a Signals struct into a class plus a
confidence, builds the clientPosture/clientTouch query string for the host,
parses the host's display_change answer, and holds the two pure decision
gates used later: UpdateGate (when a live change is worth reporting) and
RestartGate (when the stream may be resumed: setting on, 5 s arm delay, 60 s
cooldown, deferred flips are kept, baseline reset per session).

posturedetector.{h,cpp} reads the real signals. Linux asks KWin's
org.kde.KWin.TabletModeManager over D-Bus (behind HAVE_POSTURE_DBUS so builds
without QtDBus still work) and trusts tabletMode=true even when
tabletModeAvailable=false, which is what 2-in-1s report with the keyboard
detached. Windows reads SM_CONVERTIBLESLATEMODE (0 means slate), SM_DIGITIZER,
SM_MOUSEPRESENT, the chassis/DeviceForm and whether a game controller is
present (handheld). TabletModeWatcher exposes the KWin tabletModeChanged signal.

Nothing consumes this yet; it is wired in by later patches. Tests live in
tests/posture and are part of the opt-in CONFIG+=tests tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
